            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0833" n="734" xml:id="pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/2331</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3652</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-05">June 5, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        10.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction 1109 of May 29, 1936, regarding the procedure for
                    unmemorialized General Claims, and to report that on June 31 handed to the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs our note 1634 dated June 2, embodying the substance
                    of this instruction. General Hay read the note through and said that he would
                    take it under consideration immediately with a view to replying in ample time so
                    that arrangements could be made as desired by the Department before June 30.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierre de L. Boal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
